This Python function calculates the product of signs from an array of numbers. It first checks if the array is empty and returns `None` if so. Otherwise, it determines the sign based on whether any element is zero or negative. The function then multiplies the sign with the sum of absolute values of all elements in the array.

=== code written from the explanation ===

